/**
@mainpage ncr_picking Developer Reference

@section mp_overview Project Snapshot

`ncr_picking` is a Qt/C++ industrial vision-picking application. The first commercial path is
one application with explicit Commission and Runtime modes, centered on `vc::model::ITask` /
`vc::model::TaskLocalization`.

First-release integrations:
- Basler GigE camera (`vc::device::CameraBaslerGige`)
- Mitsubishi MC PLC (`vc::device::McProtocolDevice`)
- VisionOutput TCP/IP server/client (`vc::device::VisionTcpipDevice`)
- Advisory RobotKinematics checking for outgoing pick poses (`RobotKinematics::SerialRobotKinematics`)

@section mp_modules Module Map

| Module | Path | Level |
|---|---|---|
| core (settings/logger/utils) | `src/core/` | 0 |
| device | `src/device/` | 1 |
| calibration | `src/calibration/` | 1 |
| matching | `src/matching/` | 1 |
| model | `src/model/` | 2 |
| runtime | `src/runtime/` | 2 |
| ui (forms + widgets) | `src/ui/` | UI |
| app shell (+translations) | `app/` | top |
| RobotKinematics | `components/RobotKinematics/` | component |

Lower levels must not include higher ones; `model` and `runtime` may include each other;
`device` may include `calibration`; `ui` may include every non-UI module; only `app/` may
include everything. Enforced by `tests/architecture_contract_test`.

